      "title": "Brazil's SPA suspends 14 licensed betting sites over Sigap reporting and responsible-gaming control failures",
      "text": "Brazil's Secretariat of Prizes and Bets (SPA) has ordered the immediate suspension of 14 licensed betting domains after adopting seven precautionary measures, following administrative sanctioning proceedings opened in August 2025. Non-compliance carries a daily fine of BRL200,000 ($38,557). Five of the seven measures relate to failures to transmit data to Sigap, the betting management system the SPA uses to monitor betting volumes, GGR and compliance in real time; the other two concern failures to implement effective mechanisms for controlling, evaluating and monitoring users under responsible-gaming rules. Affected groups include Select Operations (mma.bet.br, betvip.bet.br, papigames.bet.br), Nexus International (megaposta.bet.br), Zeroumbet Digital Platform (zeroum.bet.br, sportvip.bet.br, energia.bet.br) and Enseada Servicos e Tecnologia (kbet.bet.br). RR Participacoes e Intermediacoes de Negocios (multibet.bet.br, rico.bet.br, brx.bet.br) was cited for failing to produce documentation supporting due diligence on its actual shareholding structure. Pixbet Solucoes Tecnologicas drew two measures - one on responsible-gaming controls and one on Sigap reporting - suspending pixbet.bet.br, ganhei.bet.br and betdasorte.bet.br. Suspended platforms may stay accessible only so players can withdraw funds. The measures rest on Articles 44-46 of Law 14.790/2023 and Articles 31-33 of SPA/MF Ordinance No. 1233/2024.",
