      "title": "Fanatics lands a multi-year NFL betting and casino partnership as the league's tri-exclusive era ends",
      "text": "Fanatics has reportedly reached a multi-year, non-exclusive agreement to become an official sports betting partner of the NFL, with Fanatics Casino also designated an official online casino partner; financial terms were not disclosed. The league and Fanatics are set to announce formally ahead of the 2026 regular season, per an unofficial press release shared with Covers. The deal covers premium NFL media inventory including in-game advertising, hospitality assets, fan experiences at the Super Bowl and other major NFL events, plus rights to league and team branding and Super Bowl and NFL draft marks. It follows the expiry earlier this year of the NFL's previous partnerships with DraftKings, FanDuel and Caesars, first announced as \"tri-exclusive\" deals in April 2021. FanDuel and DraftKings now combine for more than two-thirds of the nationwide market and have shifted emphasis toward customer value rather than share alone after absorbing hundreds of millions of dollars in losses. Fanatics Sportsbook is now available to nearly 50% of the US population, and Topps recently became the NFL's official trading card licensee. Covers notes FanDuel, DraftKings and Fanatics are each investing hundreds of millions more into their own prediction market platforms, while the NFL has been notably more cautious than other leagues and has taken no formal position on prediction markets.",
